{
  "courseId": "2511476",
  "lectureId": "15863016",
  "title": "Dictionary Keys",
  "section": 17,
  "language": "zh-Hant",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "translator": "Codex",
  "status": "complete",
  "sourceHash": "428b9ee809dbaf8021c29abe9f8e1632024873ef629ecf3496fbc39cab53d1d1",
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.48,
      "end": 1.38,
      "en": "Welcome back.",
      "zh": "歡迎回來。"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.74,
      "end": 10.02,
      "en": "I mentioned to you that a dictionary's values can hold any sort of data type, but what about the keys?",
      "zh": "我提過，字典的值可以放任何資料型別，那鍵呢？"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.14,
      "end": 15.87,
      "en": "Up until now, I've only used strings to denote a key.",
      "zh": "目前只用字串作為鍵。"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.26,
      "end": 18.47,
      "en": "But could I do something like this?",
      "zh": "但能不能這樣？"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.48,
      "end": 20.34,
      "en": "Could I do one, two, three.",
      "zh": "用 123，"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.55,
      "end": 21.48,
      "en": "Like this.",
      "zh": "像這樣。"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.83,
      "end": 23.91,
      "en": "Well, let's have a look.",
      "zh": "看看。"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.91,
      "end": 24.93,
      "en": "Let's give it a try.",
      "zh": "試試。"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.84,
      "end": 26.81,
      "en": "If I do.",
      "zh": "如果寫"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.86,
      "end": 28.21,
      "en": "One, two, three.",
      "zh": "123，"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.36,
      "end": 30.5,
      "en": "And I click Run.",
      "zh": "按 Run，"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.59,
      "end": 33.2,
      "en": "I get.",
      "zh": "得到"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.22,
      "end": 34.27,
      "en": "One, two, three.",
      "zh": "1、2、3。"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.66,
      "end": 35.14,
      "en": "Awesome.",
      "zh": "很好。"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.14,
      "end": 35.95,
      "en": "That works.",
      "zh": "能用。"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.88,
      "end": 38.08,
      "en": "What about.",
      "zh": "那麼，"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.74,
      "end": 40.15,
      "en": "What about true?",
      "zh": "True 呢？"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.6,
      "end": 42.9,
      "en": "If I select if I have a key.",
      "zh": "如果有一個鍵，"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.91,
      "end": 46.06,
      "en": "True and I click run, will that work?",
      "zh": "是 True，按 Run，能運作嗎？"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.51,
      "end": 48.04,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "可以。"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.08,
      "end": 49.31,
      "en": "It looks like it works.",
      "zh": "看起來可以。"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.34,
      "end": 50.78,
      "en": "What about a list?",
      "zh": "串列呢？"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.81,
      "end": 54.14,
      "en": "What if I have a list of, let's say, just 100?",
      "zh": "如果有個只放 100 的串列，"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.2,
      "end": 55.73,
      "en": "Would that work?",
      "zh": "能用嗎？"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.45,
      "end": 57.68,
      "en": "If I click Run?",
      "zh": "按 Run，"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.37,
      "end": 59,
      "en": "Nope.",
      "zh": "不行。"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.51,
      "end": 60.92,
      "en": "It doesn't work.",
      "zh": "不能用。"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.95,
      "end": 64.07,
      "en": "It says unhackable type list.",
      "zh": "它說 unhashable type: 'list'，串列不可雜湊。"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.19,
      "end": 65.42,
      "en": "What does that mean?",
      "zh": "什麼意思？"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.24,
      "end": 70.5,
      "en": "Dictionary keys need to have a special property.",
      "zh": "字典鍵需要具有特殊性質。"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.28,
      "end": 74.94,
      "en": "A key needs to be immutable.",
      "zh": "講者在這裡用不可變性來說明鍵的要求。"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.03,
      "end": 78.18,
      "en": "That is a key cannot change.",
      "zh": "也就是鍵不能改變。"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.72,
      "end": 81.36,
      "en": "And numbers booleans.",
      "zh": "數字、布林值，"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.36,
      "end": 84.75,
      "en": "I mean, this is a value that cannot change.",
      "zh": "這些值不能原地改變。"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.41,
      "end": 91.41,
      "en": "A string, if you remember, is a value that cannot change.",
      "zh": "記得，字串也是不能修改內容的值。"
    },
    {
      "start": 91.41,
      "end": 92.43,
      "en": "It's immutable.",
      "zh": "它不可變。"
    },
    {
      "start": 92.43,
      "end": 96.24000000000001,
      "en": "But a list, if you remember, can be changed, right?",
      "zh": "但串列可以修改，對吧？"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.24000000000001,
      "end": 103.8,
      "en": "On a list I can reassign, let's say, the index of zero to something else, right?",
      "zh": "可以把索引 0 的內容改成別的，對吧？"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.28,
      "end": 111.72,
      "en": "So because of that, a dictionary says, hey, my keys, because I'm storing them in memory and I don't want to lose them.",
      "zh": "所以字典會說：「我要把鍵存在記憶體裡，不希望弄丟它，」"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.72,
      "end": 114.69,
      "en": "It has to be something that isn't going to change on me.",
      "zh": "「因此需要不會突然改變的東西。」"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.69,
      "end": 122.31,
      "en": "Maybe a programmer comes in and by mistake changes this array of 100 to have an index of something else.",
      "zh": "也許某個程式設計師不小心，把裡面放 100 的串列，改成其他內容。"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.49,
      "end": 123.09,
      "en": "Well.",
      "zh": "那麼，"
    },
    {
      "start": 124.15,
      "end": 127.78,
      "en": "Dictionary doesn't really want that because it doesn't want to lose this value.",
      "zh": "字典不希望如此，因為不想失去對應的值。"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.93,
      "end": 131.98,
      "en": "So a dictionary key always has to be immutable.",
      "zh": "所以講者總結，字典鍵必須不可變。"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.94,
      "end": 140.95,
      "en": "And as we learn a few other things, like a couple that we'll see in upcoming videos, you can use those as keys as well.",
      "zh": "稍後學其他東西，例如即將談的 tuple 元組，也能用作鍵。"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.28,
      "end": 151.39,
      "en": "However, most of the time, 95, 99% of the time, a key for a dictionary is usually something descriptive,",
      "zh": "但多數時候，大概 95%、99% 的情況，字典鍵通常用有描述性的"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.39,
      "end": 152.41,
      "en": "like a string.",
      "zh": "字串。"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.49,
      "end": 153.79,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好。"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.79,
      "end": 156.28,
      "en": "But what about this?",
      "zh": "但這樣呢？"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.82,
      "end": 160.3,
      "en": "What if we have a another string?",
      "zh": "如果有另一個字串，"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.12,
      "end": 163.4,
      "en": "One, two, three.",
      "zh": "123，"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.97,
      "end": 165.86,
      "en": "And let's just remove this for now.",
      "zh": "先刪掉這裡。"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.97,
      "end": 171.78,
      "en": "What happens when I search for one, two, three?",
      "zh": "搜尋字串 123 時，會發生什麼？"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.81,
      "end": 172.53,
      "en": "The string.",
      "zh": "就是這個字串。"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.1,
      "end": 175.65,
      "en": "If I click run, I get.",
      "zh": "按 Run，得到"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.68,
      "end": 176.37,
      "en": "Hello?",
      "zh": "Hello。"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.03,
      "end": 189.96,
      "en": "A key in a dictionary has to be unique because there can only be one key, because that key is going to represent a bookshelf in that memory space.",
      "zh": "字典裡的鍵必須唯一，因為同一個鍵只能有一個，它代表記憶體書架上的某個位置。"
    },
    {
      "start": 190,
      "end": 196.54,
      "en": "So any time I do the same key and maybe add a value, it's going to overwrite.",
      "zh": "所以每次用相同的鍵，再指定一個值，就會覆寫。"
    },
    {
      "start": 196.54,
      "end": 198.94,
      "en": "So this no longer exists.",
      "zh": "原本的值不再對應這個鍵。"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.97,
      "end": 206.26,
      "en": "A key has to be unique and it's something that can only exist well, just once.",
      "zh": "鍵必須唯一，只能存在一次。"
    },
    {
      "start": 206.26,
      "end": 207.76,
      "en": "Otherwise we overwrite it.",
      "zh": "否則就會覆寫。"
    },
    {
      "start": 207.76,
      "end": 209.11,
      "en": "Which is why you see.",
      "zh": "所以你會看到"
    },
    {
      "start": 209.14,
      "end": 209.8,
      "en": "Hello here.",
      "zh": "這裡是 Hello。"
    },
    {
      "start": 209.8,
      "end": 211.32999999999998,
      "en": "We've lost the array.",
      "zh": "原本的串列，"
    },
    {
      "start": 211.36,
      "end": 212.95,
      "en": "One, two, three.",
      "zh": "1、2、3，已經被取代。"
    },
    {
      "start": 213.92000000000002,
      "end": 216.86,
      "en": "Let's explore this idea a little bit more in the next video.",
      "zh": "下一支影片，再多探索這個概念。"
    }
  ]
}
